import StackExchange.Puzzling139335.CornerMass.Weights

/-!
# Intrinsic corner masses of the actual Jordan pieces

At one common positive radius, every used intrinsic corner type has a
strictly positive, finite local weighted area. The sum of these areas at
each physical corner equals the area of the square in the corner ball.
Square symmetries show that the four sums are equal.

`SquareDissection.exists_positive_cornerType_weights` packages the
result as positive real weights and exact corner incidence identities.
No sector angle or zero-area-boundary assumption is used.
-/
